  "id": "open-land-idle",
  "name": "Play a land on turn 1-2 when nothing in hand unlocks anything",
  "intent": "On turn 1 or 2, once none of open-land-unlocks, open-shock-unlocks, open-fetch-unlocks or open-fetch-unlocks-shock apply and no other hand card is already affordable, still play the land drop - any land in hand beats holding it back with nothing to protect. Prefers a surveil land (Thundering Falls) first and keeps the surveilled card, since it was entering tapped regardless and the scry is free value; then any other land that would enter tapped anyway (none exists in this manabase today, but the tier stays for a future addition and costs nothing to keep); then a shockland, life declined - a paid shockland is real mana this turn, strictly better to hold open than an already-untapped fetch that produces nothing until cracked (item 9, 2026-09-14 review batch, swapping the old fetch-before-shock order); then a fetch, held everywhere else for a target-rich turn but taken here since nothing else is better. The false list's own fetch keys narrow/extend to match F's own narrowed unlocks_by_basic_search true key plus the new open-fetch-unlocks-shock play's own broader unlocks_by_search true key (item 4), so this play only stands down for either once it would actually fire. Only turns 1-2, land drop available, mine, precombat main, empty stack.",
